            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Neither is better everywhere. Evaporative humidifiers suit hard water, large rooms and people who want low upkeep, because minerals stay in the wick and output slows as the room gets humid. Ultrasonic humidifiers suit bedrooms and light sleepers because they are nearly silent, but they work best with distilled or very soft water."
