        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The deciding question between an evaporative and an ultrasonic humidifier is not which technology is newer. It is what is in your water and how much noise you will tolerate. Hard water and a desire for low upkeep point to evaporative. Soft or distilled water and a quiet bedroom point to ultrasonic.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever you choose, set a humidity target of 30 to 50 percent, refill with fresh water every day and clean the tank weekly. Those habits matter more to your air than the type of machine on the dresser.
          </p>
        </div>

